# Agent CLIs to install.
#
# Read by scripts/install-local-clis.sh when you pass no CLI names, and by the
# Docker image build (the Dockerfile copies this file). One id per line, or
# several separated by commas or spaces. Blank lines and anything after `#`
# are ignored.
#
# Leave every id commented out to install the historical default set:
#   local script — claude, codex, gemini, opencode, openclaw
#   Docker image — those five, plus cursor, hermes, fx and antigravity
#
# Uncomment a subset to install only those. Claude and Codex stay required
# when they are selected: a failed install stops the local run and fails the
# image build. Every other CLI stays best-effort, so a vendor CDN being down
# does not fail the build. Omitting claude or codex skips them; it does not
# fail the run.
#
# AM_INSTALL_CLIS overrides this file when it is set and not empty
# (`AM_INSTALL_CLIS=claude,cursor ./scripts/install-local-clis.sh`, or
# `docker build --build-arg AM_INSTALL_CLIS=claude,cursor`). A Space variable
# of the same name is injected at runtime, after the image exists, so it
# cannot skip an install — commit this file (or pass the build arg) and
# rebuild. Ids are the catalog ids. `agy` and `cursor-agent` are accepted
# aliases.
#
# Example: Claude Code and Cursor only, and nothing else (Codex, Hermes,
# OpenClaw, fx, Antigravity, Gemini, opencode):
#
# claude
# cursor

# claude
# codex
# gemini
# opencode
# openclaw
# cursor
# hermes
# fx
# antigravity
